        "rationale": "[recovery-agent diagnosis via claude-opus-5[1m]] TG_REVIEW / tg_gate_cause=breakpoint_ambiguity at 100 K/ns, reported by extract_thermal as 69.7 K (> 20 K). That is the larger of the breakpoint spread (69.7 K, 11 splits within 10% of the best SSR) and 2 x sigma (2 x 19.6 K). Tg_K=572.4 K, Tg_alternative_K=519.1 K. The bilinear fit is GOOD (R\u00b2=0.9841), and all 27 temperatures passed per-T sampling. workflow_state.json shows no remedy applied (remedy_counters.total=0, no agent_escalations). The tg_breakpoint remedy declined: halving tg_t_step_K 20 to 10 at 100 K/ns gives 100000 steps/T, below PKTN's tg_min_steps_per_T=200000 (the 1.00x-floor case documented in workflow_engine._tg_review).\n\nRoot cause is the pre-registered outcome in guides/polymer_rules.json PKTN _tg_slope_gate_note (line 1862). On 2026-09-01 the rigid-aromatic cold-start artifact was 'fixed' by starting the sweep from the melt-cooled cell, which re-armed the method-gap gate. The note says the next PEEK run TESTS that fix: 'If the >20 K gap ... returns, the diagnosis was wrong and the cause is not the cold start -- restore tg_slope_gate_fallback=\"slowest_rate\" rather than widening the gate.' PEEK_2 did start from the melt (tg_start_cell.outcome=MELT_HOLD_START, T_start 770 K, tg_melt_start_density_consistent=true), and the gap returned at 69.7 K. The remedy the class note prescribes is a class-config change (restore a polymer_rules.json key). Separately, method_gap_exempt is hardcoded False in stage_params.py:876. Neither is a decided_params override, so this needs a human.\n\nThe only in-contract lever is lowering tg_rate_K_per_ns (e.g. 50). Priced on this run's wall times, it is poor value. EXTRA_INVALIDATION re-runs cooling (3.0 h) plus thermal (5.6 h), roughly doubled to about 17 h. The memory record for PEEK4 (PKTN/PCFF) shows seed-to-seed MD Tg scatter of 496-563 K across 9 GOOD/EXCELLENT sweeps, the same size as this 69.7 K spread. So one slower sweep is unlikely to bring the spread under 20 K. The density staircase shows flat pairs (710/690, 590/570, 510/490 K), consistent with noise rather than an under-resolved grid. remedy_economics.py could not be run (the Bash call needed approval in this headless session), so no SPEND verdict exists to justify the rung.\n\nHuman options: (1) restore tg_slope_gate_fallback='slowest_rate' for PKTN/PSFO and decide whether to re-plumb method_gap_exempt; (2) accept and annotate MD Tg ~520-570 K with the documented PCFF aromatic-ketone overprediction (exp 418 K); (3) deliberately spend a 50 K/ns cooling + sweep rung (~17 h)."
      },
